parts.text:
Now need test setup screenshot. Could potentially use `QQuickWindow` in offscreen and app automation by modifying seeded DB? For map setup, we can test the same provider and grab in a standalone test. Let's build a temporary test with QGuiApplication + QQuickView loading `qml/MapCanvas.qml` from source. It needs image provider. We can compile a small test target in /tmp using core library or just add a temporary target not committed? We can create `/tmp/maptest/CMakeLists.txt` linking poisonlog_core and Qt6 Quick, loading source QML file. The source map canvas hardcodes image://tiles. Add provider. Then set properties via root object; wait for tilesReady; call grabToImage QML? Easier C++ `QQuickItem::grabToImage` then QSignalSpy? `QQuickItemGrabResult` save. But need QQuickView offscreen (QGuiApplication). Could compile with cmake referencing project core static lib. Let's do temporary in /tmp (allowed). Not part of repo.

Test program:
```cpp
#include <QGuiApplication>
#include <QQuickView>
#include <QQmlEngine>
#include <QQuickItemGrabResult>
#include <QTimer>
#include "tileimageprovider.h"
int main... {
 QGuiApplication app;
 QQuickView view;
 view.engine()->addImageProvider("tiles", new TileImageProvider);
 view.setSource(QUrl::fromLocalFile("/home/.../qml/MapCanvas.qml"));
 view.resize(768,768); view.show();
 auto *item = view.rootObject();
 item->setProperty("centerLat",38.8976); item->setProperty("centerLon",-77.0365); item->setProperty("active",true);
 QTimer poll; check tilesReady property; when true, item->grabToImage(QSize(768,768)); connect result ready? QQuickItem::grabToImage returns QSharedPointer<QQuickItemGrabResult> and result has ready signal. Save file.
```
Need QML import path for QtQuick; engine will find via Qt qml path. MapCanvas qml imports QtQuick only, so can load local file directly. Great. Need event loop. Timeout 30s. Verify file exists and image not blank.

Compile with qmake? Use g++ with pkg? Better temporary CMake find Qt6. Use Qt CMake. We can create /tmp/maptest with CMakeLists linking `/home/dwight/git/poisonlog/build/libpoisonlog_core.a` and Qt6::Quick/Network. Need include src. The core library includes TileImageProvider (QQuickImageProvider). Link Qt6::Quick etc. Maybe easiest compile test source directly with g++ and pkg-config from Qt? Qt has no pkg-config. Use CMake.

We'll write temp and build. This is extra but verifies critical map path. Let's do.

